  "problems": "Diesel's own site (uk.diesel.com and diesel.com/en-us, women's jeans product pages, 'Size chart' panel) shows only a conversion table (Diesel Size / Intern. Size / Ita / Us / De / Fr/Es / Uk / Ru) with no waist or hip measurements; the women's denim guide (global.diesel.com/woman/denim-guide/) describes fits only. The table is staggered: Diesel sizes 23, 25, 27-31 and 33 each straddle two rows of the conversion columns, so those aliases are recorded as 'A/B' exactly as the spans fall (e.g. 28 spans IT 42 and 44). measurement_basis and unit are null because no measurements exist. Third-party sites (footshop.eu, size-charts.com) publish waist/hip cm values labelled as Diesel, but they are not the brand's chart and were not used. Extra alias keys used: it, de, fr, uk, ru."
